  m_Name: 1.Intro
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Readme
  icon: {fileID: 0}
  title: Procedural Progress Bars
  sections:
  - heading: Introduction + Overview
    text: "Compatibility\n\nThis asset supports Unity 6.0 and above, with Shader
      Graph shaders support URP and HDRP. All shaders are created using Shader Graph.\n\nSupports:\n\u2022
      Canvas Shader \u2013 optimized for UI elements.\n\u2022 Unlit Shader \u2013
      ideal for world space usage.\n\nIMPORT & SETUP \n\nImporting the Asset [[IMAGE:0]]\n\n\nDemo
      Scenes\n\nTwo showcase scenes are included in this checkout to showcase usage
      examples and features.\n\nFind them under:\n\nAssets/ThirdParty/CupOHappiness/ProceduralProgressBars/Demo
      Scenes\n\nIncluded scenes: `Demo Scenes/Features Showcase.unity` and `Demo
      Scenes/Styles Showcase.unity`.\n[[IMAGE:1]]\n\n\n\nSee the Quick Start section.\n\nOverview\n\nThis asset revolves around three key components:\n\u2022
      ProceduralProgressBar.cs \u2013 The main controller script.\n\u2022 Procedural
      Progress Bar Canvas Shader \u2013 Designed for UI Image components.\n\u2022
      Procedural Progress Bar Unlit Shader \u2013 Designed for 3D world space meshes.\n\nAll
      shaders are built with Shader Graph and provided here for URP.\n\u2705 Use
      the Canvas shader for UI elements (like Unity UI Image).\\\n\u2705 Use the
      Unlit shader for 3D meshes (like planes or quads in world space)."
